  "proof_summary": "Retain the full original theorem for every nonzero natural level N, every prime ell not dividing N, and every valuation subring A of the algebraic closure of Q lying over ell. It constructs the original AlgebraicCurve.RegularProlongation from modularFunctionFieldBar N to modularFunctionFieldFullC over the residue field and proves, for every integral Laurent series y with the original membership hypothesis, that its lift lies in the prolongation integer ring and its residue equals the coefficientwise residue series. The original integer-ring, residue homomorphism, surjectivity, kernel, scalar compatibility, denominator clearing, finite-rank transport and final assembly proofs are preserved. No additional restriction is introduced. Canonical source/card remain byte-identical to their supplier originals. Original warnings are retained; separate final solution axiom audit remains pending.",
